    "title": "Odessa files 2024-2025 city audit on time for first time in 8 years - NewsBreak",
    "text": "20 hours ago The Odessa City Council has approved the 2024–2025 fiscal year audit on time — the first time the city has met the state’s 180‑day audit deadline since 2017–2018 . Mayor Cal Hendrick said the city’s finance department had struggled in recent years after losing staff, which caused delays and cost Odessa its bond rating. Completing the audit on schedule helps restore financial credibility and keeps the city in compliance with state law. Hendrick noted that the process even uncovered unaccounted funds that will now support local infrastructure projects. City leaders say they plan to keep audits a top priority moving forward.\nMore Info: Odessa city council approves 2024-2025 year audit ...\n1",
